Can you also show the summary from the new result?
And also the convergence plot before and after?
Then I might be able to say more.

The bru_verbose output in the two cases would also help.

Gamma is involved with both beta and the iid effects, which may be why setting gamma nonzero helps; it makes the initial derivatives with respect to beta and the iid effects nonzero. Normally, that would be sorted out in the second iteration once gamma gets a nonzero value from the other likelihood, so it should have been ok. The verbose output and diagnostics may help explain.

Finn

